    <!--
        2026-08-28: REMOVED the Task <objectPermissions> block that lived here. This is not a
        typo or a missed deploy — it is IMPOSSIBLE to grant on this platform, proven, not
        assumed: ObjectPermissions.SobjectType is a RESTRICTED PICKLIST of 3,007 values, and
        Task, Event and Activity are NOT among them (Account/Contact/Lead/Opportunity/Case/
        Contract all are). A direct API insert of an ObjectPermissions row for Task returns
        INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST on SobjectType — Task CRUD can only be granted
        via a PROFILE, which is ruled out for this org.

        Worse, leaving the block in this file was actively misleading: Salesforce ACCEPTS it on
        deploy and reports the component as Changed, then SILENTLY DISCARDS it. Measured
        2026-08-28 on usman-dpeg: deploy of this exact block reported success, and a readback of
        the deployed permission set showed 35 fieldPermissions present and ZERO
        objectPermissions. Do not re-add this block believing the earlier absence was a bug or
        an unfinished deploy.

        The replacement authorization path is the Transaction_Task_Actions custom permission
        (granted above via <customPermissions>), which TransactionTaskService reads via
        FeatureManagement.checkPermission before running its Task-completion DML in system mode.
        Sharing is unaffected by this — only object-level CRUD is bypassed, and only on that one
        write path. See customPermissions/Transaction_Task_Actions.customPermission-meta.xml for
        the full rationale.
    -->
